  "description": "traffic-network.md §2.7.2-§2.7.3 (TS6): messages 0x8A0D15DA / 0xEA0D163E with data1 type, data2 x, data3 z. Add finds the connection (FindConnection), sets the mask bit, raises the cost to commuteMaxTime (90.0) or to the other side's 0xCA947077 (120.0) - the cost only grows - and gives the record the pool of the established city on the other side, found by position or created under the smallest unused ID >= 1; a city that is not established gives pool 0; no connection of the type: nothing. Remove clears the type; the last type also sets pool 0, runs the pool sweep (pool 2 released), decrements freeDest once per set destination bit (0b1011 at (8, 2)) and zeroes the byte; the cost stays. Removing one of two types changes nothing else. B's next Add creates pool 2 again.",
